course: dictionary
lesson: 9193
title: One word, different meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Context, the words around it, tells you which meaning the writer means. The word «soda» is a good example, because it can mean a drink, a kind of water, or a white powder.
explain: «A can of soda left too long in the freezer can bulge and burst.» A can holds a drink, so here soda means a sweet fizzy drink, also called pop or soft drink. In «The acid in the vinegar and the alkali in the soda react», soda is a powder, not a drink. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then swap your meaning in and check it still makes sense.
explain: Some sentences show a different job for the same word. «Sand is melted with soda and crushed limestone in a furnace» tells you that soda is something added to sand to make glass. You would not drink it. The clues are melted, furnace and glass sheets, bottles and jars.
fact: A word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which meaning is used.
fact: «Soda» can mean a sweet fizzy drink, also called pop or soft drink.
fact: «Soda water» is water with bubbles and no sugar.
fact: «Baking soda» is a white powder used in baking and cleaning.
fact: In science, «baking soda» and vinegar react and make carbon dioxide gas, which bubbles out.
exercise: «A can of soda left too long in the freezer can bulge and burst.» What is soda here? | A glass bottle for milk | * A fizzy drink in a can | A small cloud of steam | A white powder used for baking
exercise: «The acid in the vinegar and the alkali in the soda react and make a new substance.» What does react mean? | * Mix and change into something new | Stay exactly the same | Taste sweet | Freeze solid
exercise: Which of these is soda water? | Frozen cola | * Water with bubbles and no sugar | Thick, sweet syrup | Melted glass
test: «Sand is melted with soda and crushed limestone in a furnace hotter than 1000 °C.» What is the soda used to make? | Pop | Ice cream | Cakes | * Glass
test: Jade says, «I'll add soda to my cake batter.» Which kind of soda should she use? | * Baking soda | Soda water | Diet soda | A can of soda
exam: «Blueberries turn greenish in batter with too much baking soda.» In this sentence, what is baking soda? | A glass bottle | * A white powder used in baking | A sweet fizzy drink | Water with bubbles and no sugar
